_id: 102\n    description: \"Office area with desk - third checkpoint\"\n\n  - name: \"Storage\"\n    position:\n      x: -3.8\n      y: 4.6    # extra clearance from divider/shelf to reduce local oscillation\n      z: 0.0\n    orientation:\n      x: 0.0\n      y: 0.0\n      z: 0.447   # Face marker from standoff position (~53 degrees yaw)\n      w: 0.894\n    marker_id: 103\n    description: \"Storage room with shelves - fourth checkpoint\"\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"035a7608-a82f-45f9-88aa-b2dc5c7f6188"}
{"parentUuid":"5a8d61a8-2ead-4dba-801b-a11f972c6efd","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/denis/ros2_ws/src","sessionId":"7525ea68-9b14-4c16-85a8-3d457837ea00","version":"2.1.38","gitBranch":"main","slug":"rustling-munching-cook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Tvv7WPHRCyHw2iYnAhEWqS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the screenshot more carefully and correlate with the params.\n\nFrom the screenshot:\n1. The robot appears to be at the bottom of the map (near the bottom-right area based on the sensor data)\n2. The path (red curve) seems to go from bottom towards the middle\n3. There are large cyan rectangular obstacles (shelves/furniture) with massive pink inflation zones\n4. The robot has done 3 recoveries in 122 seconds\n\nKey issues I can identify from the parameters:\n\n1. **Global costmap inflation_radius: 0.65** with **cost_scaling_factor: 3.2** — This is creating very large inflated zones. With a robot footprint of ~0.36m (half-length), an inflation radius of 0.65m means the total clearance from obstacles is 0.65m. \n\nIn narrow corridors, this could make passages appear nearly blocked.\n\n2. **Local costmap inflation_radius: 0.45** with **cost_scaling_factor: 4.0** — This is also quite aggressive.\n\n3. **BaseObstacle.scale: 0.20** — This is very low. The robot isn't being penalized much for being near obstacles in trajectory selection, which could lead to oscillation near obstacles.\n\n4. **DWB sim_time: 1.2** — With max_vel_x of 0.30, this only looks 0.36m ahead. This is quite short.\n\n5. **max_vel_x: 0.30** — The robot's maximum forward velocity is quite conservative, which combined with the short lookahead distance, limits how far ahead the planner can see.\n\nLooking at the screenshot, the cyan rectangles represent shelving units and the pink inflation zones around them are creating bottlenecks that the robot struggles to navigate through. The red path shows the planner attempting to thread through these narrow corridors, and the three recovery attempts suggest it's getting stuck or oscillating when trying to find a viable route. The global inflation radius of 0.65m is likely the primary culprit here, as it's too aggressive for the tight spaces between shelves. The inflation radius of 0.65m is creating a keep-out zone that's too large for a 2m-wide corridor, leaving barely any navigable space once both walls are inflated. This tight constraint is forcing the global planner into inefficient curved paths and causing the local planner to fail repeatedly, triggering those recovery behaviors. I should walk through the specific parameter trade-offs rather than just suggesting changes, since this is a learning exercise.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":934,"cache_read_input_tokens":41739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":934},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CY2Sy5sFVSN8HFFcE2oFf","type":"assistant","uuid":"14044685-f149-4eca-af94-333da224510e","timestamp":"2026-02-11T14:35:43.027Z"}
