{"parentUuid":"3adee93a-a29a-45c3-8ef8-64a6cc1edb2a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/denis/ros2_ws/src","sessionId":"7525ea68-9b14-4c16-85a8-3d457837ea00","version":"2.1.38","gitBranch":"main","slug":"rustling-munching-cook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BWETxHBC6XMbvDYeRbfBNC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a much clearer picture. Let me analyze the key issues:\n\nThe office has two internal dividers:\n- **wall_divider_1** at x=1, y=1, 0.2m thick × 6m long — creates a corridor between it and the east wall\n- **wall_divider_2** at x=-4, y=1, 0.2m thick × 5m long — creates a corridor between it and the west wall\n\nThese dividers create narrow corridors/passages. Looking at the RViz screenshot, the cyan rectangles are likely these dividers seen in the costmap.\n\nLet me calculate the corridor widths:\n\n\n- Between wall_divider_1 (x=1) and wall_east (x=8): 7m wide — plenty of room\n- Between wall_divider_2 (x=-4) and wall_west (x=-8): 4m wide — still decent\n- Between wall_divider_1 (x=1) and wall_divider_2 (x=-4): 5m wide — also decent\n\nThe cyan shapes in the RViz screenshot are the internal dividers themselves, and the pink inflation around them is quite substantial. Looking more closely at the visualization, there seem to be additional structural elements I'm not immediately accounting for.\n\nThe two long thin dividers are separated by 5m, and even accounting for the 0.65m inflation radius on each side, that should leave roughly 3.3m of navigable space between them — which should be more than enough. But the pink inflation zones appear much larger than expected in the screenshot. The real constraint might not be the corridor width itself, but rather the length of these dividers extending through the Y direction, which could force the robot to navigate around their endpoints rather than straight through.\n\nLooking at the red path in the screenshot, it curves around the bottom of the dividers, suggesting the robot is trying to navigate from the south side to reach the goal by going around the barrier ends. The three recovery attempts indicate it's getting stuck at bottleneck points where the inflation zones create tight passages, likely near where the dividers terminate.\n\nThe robot has been navigating for 122 seconds with 3.61m remaining, and those repeated recovery behaviors suggest the local planner is struggling to find valid trajectories through the narrow inflated zones. The main culprit appears to be the global costmap's inflation radius of 0.65m, which combined with the robot's 0.36m half-length creates an overly conservative keep-out zone of roughly 1.0m from obstacles—making those gaps around the divider ends nearly impassable.\n\nThe cost scaling factors (3.2 globally, 4.0 locally) are also working against us by extending the penalized zone well beyond the inflation radius itself. Meanwhile, the DWB BaseObstacle critic is set too low at 0.20, so it's not strongly discouraging the robot from getting close to obstacles in the first place, which then causes the inflation layer to abruptly block it and trigger oscillation. The collision monitor's 0.8-second time-before-collision threshold is also quite conservative—at the robot's 0.30 m/s speed, that means it starts braking 0.24m out, which in tight spaces compounds the problem and nearly stops the robot.\n\nThe simulation horizon of 1.2 seconds for DWB is also too short; it only projects 0.36m ahead at max velocity, so the robot can't adequately plan through narrow passages. I need to work through these parameters systematically and come up with concrete adjustments.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2061,"cache_read_input_tokens":42673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2061},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CY2T1u6gW9yhftJaDJqR9","type":"assistant","uuid":"865b0628-a3c4-4b60-8371-ede9e386dbb6","timestamp":"2026-02-11T14:36:23.942Z"}
{"parentUuid":"865b0628-a3c4-4b60-8371-ede9e386dbb6","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/denis/ros2_ws/src","sessionId":"7525ea68-9b14-4c16-85a8-3d457837ea00","version":"2.1.38","gitBranch":"main","slug":"rustling-munching-cook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BWETxHBC6XMbvDYeRbfBNC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bien, ya tengo toda la información necesaria. Aquí está mi diagnóstico:\n\n---\n\n## Diagnóstico de la Navegación\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n**Cómo funciona la inflación en Nav2**: El `inflation_layer` crea un gradiente de costo alrededor de cada obstáculo. El `inflation_radius` define el radio total de la zona penalizada, y el `cost_scaling_factor` controla qué tan rápido decae el costo con la distancia. Un factor **bajo** = el costo cae **lentamente** (zona penalizada más \"dura\"). Un factor **alto** = el costo cae **rápido** (solo penaliza cerca del obstáculo).\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n### Lo que veo en la captura\n\n1. **Recoveries: 3** en solo 122 segundos — el local planner (DWB) no encuentra trayectorias válidas repetidamente\n2. **Zonas de inflación enormes (rosa)** — las paredes divisoras (`wall_divider_1` y `wall_divider_2`) generan zonas infladas que estrechan los pasajes\n3. **Trayectoria curva ineficiente** — el global planner hace un rodeo largo para evitar las zonas infladas\n4. **122s para ~3.6m restantes** — velocidad efectiva muy baja por las recuperaciones constantes\n\n### Causas raíz identificadas\n\n| Parámetro | Valor actual | Problema |\n|-----------|-------------|----------|\n| `global_costmap.inflation_radius` | **0.65m** | Muy alto. Con footprint de 0.36m y paredes, los pasillos se cierran casi completamente |\n| `global_costmap.cost_scaling_factor` | **3.2** | Bajo = el costo decae lentamente → zona penalizada \"dura\" y amplia |\n| `local_costmap.inflation_radius` | **0.45m** | También agresivo para el local planner, causa que DWB no encuentre trayectorias |\n| `DWB BaseObstacle.scale` | **0.20** | Muy bajo → el robot no evita obstáculos con anticipación y luego se queda atrapado en la zona inflada |\n| `DWB sim_time` | **1.2s** | A 0.30 m/s solo proyecta 0.36m adelante → no \"ve\" a través de pasillos estrechos |\n| `collision_monitor.time_before_collision` | **0.8s** | Conservador → frena 0.24m antes de colisión, compuesto con la inflación paraliza al robot |\n\n### El ciclo vicioso\n\n```\nInflación grande → pasillo estrecho → DWB no encuentra trayectoria →\n→ Recovery (spin/backup) → nuevo intento → misma situación → Recovery...\n```\n\n---\n\n### Ajustes recomendados\n\nEsto es un balance entre **seguridad** (no chocar) y **navegabilidad** (poder pasar por los pasillos). Te propongo los cambios, pero hay una decisión de diseño importante que quiero consultarte:\n\nEl robot tiene un footprint de 0.72m × 0.34m. Los divisores crean pasillos de ~5m de ancho, pero las paredes del perímetro crean esquinas más estrechas. Hay dos filosofías:\n\n1. **Reducir inflación agresivamente** — Más navegable pero el robot pasa más cerca de obstáculos. Riesgo: rozar paredes en giros.\n2. **Reducir inflación moderadamente + mejorar DWB** — Mantener algo de margen pero hacer el planner más inteligente para navegar espacios estrechos.\n\nTe recomiendo la opción 2. Los cambios clave serían:\n\n```yaml\n# Global costmap - reducir inflación pero mantener seguridad\ninflation_radius: 0.50      # era 0.65 → reduce zona total sin sacrificar seguridad\ncost_scaling_factor: 5.0     # era 3.2 → costo decae más rápido, menos penalización lejos del obstáculo\n\n# Local costmap  \ninflation_radius: 0.35      # era 0.45 → DWB encuentra más trayectorias válidas\ncost_scaling_factor: 6.0     # era 4.0 → deja el centro del pasillo más \"libre\"\n\n# DWB - mejor capacidad de navegar espacios estrechos\nsim_time: 2.0               # era 1.2 → proyecta ~0.6m adelante, ve a través de pasillos\nBaseObstacle.scale: 0.50    # era 0.20 → evita obstáculos con más anticipación\nvx_samples: 16              # era 12 → más opciones de velocidad\n\n# Collision monitor - menos conservador\ntime_before_collision: 0.5  # era 0.8 → frena 0.15m antes en vez de 0.24m\n```\n\n¿Quieres que aplique estos cambios? ¿O prefieres un enfoque más agresivo (opción 1) que reduzca la inflación más?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2061,"cache_read_input_tokens":42673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2061},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CY2T1u6gW9yhftJaDJqR9","type":"assistant","uuid":"e900cc4e-e805-4f5a-87c0-74b65cdca8cf","timestamp":"2026-02-11T14:36:46.755Z"}
