{"parentUuid":"6b58f2ab-12bd-44bd-a70d-02dd6184055f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/denis/ros2_ws/src","sessionId":"7525ea68-9b14-4c16-85a8-3d457837ea00","version":"2.1.38","gitBranch":"main","slug":"rustling-munching-cook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ADTaxsiyPFvSnKoQCaMW8N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The flow is clear. The `go2_autonav.sh` passes:\n- `world_init_x:=$INIT_X` where `INIT_X=-2.0`\n- `world_init_y:=$INIT_Y` where `INIT_Y=-1.6`\n- `world_init_z:=$SPAWN_Z` where `SPAWN_Z=0.40`\n- `world_init_heading:=$INIT_YAW` where `INIT_YAW=-1.57`\n\nAnd in the launch file `unitree_go2_launch.py`, these are passed to `ros2 run ros_gz_sim create` (the spawner):\n\n\n- `-x` world_init_x\n- `-y` world_init_y\n- `-z` world_init_z\n- `-Y` world_init_heading\n\nSo the robot spawns at (-2.0, -1.6, 0.40) with heading -1.57 facing the -Y direction. Looking at the Gazebo screenshot, the robot's position matches that corner location, and the Lobby waypoint is at x=-2.0, y=-1, which is very close to the spawn point.\n\nThe spawn position aligns with the first waypoint on the patrol route, so the robot starts ready to begin its mission immediately. The user might be wondering why it doesn't start at the origin or elsewhere, but this placement makes sense given the waypoint layout.\n\nLooking at the corridor structure, the spawn point at (-2.0, -1.6) sits between the two dividing walls in the middle corridor, positioned toward the southern end of the map—which tracks as the Lobby area. The user might be asking because they're seeing unexpected behavior with where the robot actually appears in the simulation.\n\nThe initialization coordinates are set in the startup script, hardcoded to match the Lobby waypoint so the robot begins its patrol route from that first designated location.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_t