{"parentUuid":"ceb9380f-b056-475b-a59b-cb1f38a47cca","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/denis/ros2_ws/src","sessionId":"7525ea68-9b14-4c16-85a8-3d457837ea00","version":"2.1.38","gitBranch":"main","slug":"rustling-munching-cook","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015kwnXRDtN2GQHW7PLrAmJg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# CLAUDE.md\n     2→\n     3→This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n     4→\n     5→## Project Overview\n     6→\n     7→Autonomous industrial inspection system using a Unitree Go2 quadruped robot with Nav2 navigation and ArUco marker detection, running on **ROS 2 Jazzy** / **Ubuntu 24.04** with **Gazebo Harmonic** simulation.\n     8→\n     9→The robot patrols 4 office waypoints (Lobby, Corridor, Office, Storage), navigates via Nav2, and verifies ArUco markers (IDs 100-103, DICT_4X4_1000) at each checkpoint. Results are logged to CSV with images.\n    10→\n    11→## Build & Test Commands\n    12→\n    13→All commands run from `~/ros2_ws`:\n    14→\n    15→```bash\n    16→colcon build --symlink-install                                    # build all\n    17→colcon build --symlink-install --packages-select <package>        # build one package\n    18→source install/setup.bash                                         # source after every build\n    19→colcon test --packages-select aruco_markers                       # run aruco tests (GTest)\n    20→aruco_markers/scripts/unit_test.sh                                # run aruco unit tests directly\n    21→aruco_markers/scripts/format.sh                                   # C++ formatting (ament_uncrustify)\n    22→```\n    23→\n    24→## Launch Sequence (4 terminals, source workspace in each)\n    25→\n    26→```bash\n    27→# T1: Simulation\n    28→ros2 launch unitree_go2_sim unitree_go2_launch.py world:=office_patrol.sdf\n    29→\n    30→# T2: Navigation (AMCL + Nav2)\n    31→ros2 launch unitree_go2_sim nav2_patrol_launch.py map:=~/ros2_ws/src/unitree_go2_ros2/maps/office_patrol_map.yaml\n    32→\n    33→# T3: ArUco detection\n    34→ros2 launch unitree_go2_sim aruco_detection_launch.py\n    35→\n    36→# T4: Patrol controller\n    37→ros2 run unitree_go2_sim patrol_controller.py\n    38→```\n    39→\n    40→Or use the all-in-one script: `~/ros2_ws/src/Scripts/go2_autonav.sh`\n    41→\n    42→Kill everything: `GO2_KILL_GZ=1 ~/ros2_ws/src/Scripts/go2_kill_terms.sh`\n    43→\n    44→## Package Structure\n    45→\n    46→- **`aruco_markers/aruco_markers/`** — C++ node for ArUco detection using OpenCV. Source in `src/`, headers in `include/aruco_markers/`, tests in `test/` (GTest).\n    47→- **`aruco_markers/aruco_markers_msgs/`** — Custom messages: `Marker` (id, pose, pixel coords) and `MarkerArray`.\n    48→- **`unitree_go2_ros2/unitree_go2_sim/`** — Launch files (`launch/`), Python scripts (`scripts/` — patrol_controller, camera_info_publisher), config YAML (`config/`).\n    49→- **`unitree_go2_ros2/unitree_go2_description/`** — URDF/xacro (`urdf/`), Gazebo worlds (`worlds/`), ArUco marker models (`models/`), meshes.\n    50→- **`unitree_go2_ros2/champ/`** + **`champ_base/`** — CHAMP quadruped locomotion framework and ROS drivers (controller, state estimation, EKF).\n    51→- **`unitree_go2_ros2/config/`** — Nav2 params (`nav2_go2_params.yaml`), SLAM params, RViz configs.\n    52→- **`Scripts/`** — Bash launcher scripts: `go2_autonav.sh` (all-in-one), `go2_launcher.sh` (base launcher), `go2_nav2_map.sh` (nav2+map), `go2_patrol_nav.sh` (patrol nav), `go2_kill_terms.sh` (kill all), `go2_reset_localization.sh` (reset AMCL pose).\n    53→\n    54→## Architecture\n    55→\n    56→**Control stack**: Gazebo Harmonic → ros_gz_bridge → CHAMP quadruped controller → Dual EKF filters → Nav2 (AMCL + DWB local planner)\n    57→\n    58→**TF tree**: `map` → (AMCL) → `odom` → (EKF) → `base_link` → `base_footprint` → leg links\n    59→\n    60→**Sensor pipeline**: Velodyne PointCloud2 → `pointcloud_to_laserscan` → `/scan` (LaserScan) → Nav2 costmaps\n    61→\n    62→**ArUco pipeline**: `/rgb_image` + `/rgb_image/camera_info` → `aruco_markers` node → `/aruco/markers` (MarkerArray) + `/aruco/result` (debug image)\n    63→\n    64→**Patrol controller** (`patrol_controller.py`): Python node using `nav2_simple_commander.BasicNavigator`. Navigates waypoints, polls `/aruco/markers`, retries up to 3 times with optional in-place rotation, logs to CSV at `~/inspection_data/`.\n    65→\n    66→## Coding Conventions\n    67→\n    68→- **Python**: PEP 8, 4-space indent, `snake_case` functions/vars, `CamelCase` classes\n    69→- **C++**: Format with `aruco_markers/scripts/format.sh` (ament_uncrustify)\n    70→- **ROS 2**: Package names `lowercase_with_underscores`, topics `/lowercase/with/slashes`\n    71→- **All packages**: `ament_cmake` build system\n    72→\n    73→## Commit Style\n    74→\n    75→Short imperative summaries (e.g., \"Add ...\", \"Fix ...\", \"Adjust ...\"). Add body for multi-area changes. Include affected packages and commands run (`colcon build`, `colcon test`).\n    76→\n    77→## Key Configuration Files\n    78→\n    79→| File | Purpose |\n    80→|------|---------|\n    81→| `unitree_go2_sim/config/nav2_go2_params.yaml` | Nav2 parameters (AMCL, DWB, costmaps) — canonical source (`unitree_go2_ros2/config/` has symlinks) |\n    82→| `unitree_go2_sim/config/patrol_waypoints.yaml` | Patrol waypoints with marker IDs |\n    83→| `unitree_go2_sim/config/gait/gait.yaml` | Quadruped gait parameters |\n    84→| `unitree_go2_sim/config/ros_control/ros_control.yaml` | Joint controllers (250 Hz) |\n    85→| `unitree_go2_description/worlds/office_patrol.sdf` | Gazebo world with ArUco markers |\n    86→\n    87→## Important Runtime Notes\n    88→\n    89→- Always `source install/setup.bash` in every terminal before launching\n    90→- Set `GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH` to include `unitree_go2_description/models` if marker models are missing (launcher scripts handle this)\n    91→- Set initial pose in RViz (\"2D Pose Estimate\") before starting patrol\n    92→- ArUco markers are 300mm code on 340mm panel (20mm quiet zone), placed at ground level\n    93→- Waypoints are offset ~0.9m from marker positions to stay outside Nav2 inflation radius\n    94→- Robot radius: 0.30m, max velocity: 0.30 m/s forward, 0.50 rad/s rotation (tuned to CHAMP gait limits)\n    95→- Inspection output: `~/inspection_data/inspection_log.csv` + `~/inspection_data/images/`\n    96→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"uuid":"e26bf03d-c721-4bcb-bd90-cca1a906db59","timestamp":"2026-02-11T16:12:37.080Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/denis/ros2_ws/src/CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nAutonomous industrial inspection system using a Unitree Go2 quadruped robot with Nav2 navigation and ArUco marker detection, running on **ROS 2 Jazzy** / **Ubuntu 24.04** with **Gazebo Harmonic** simulation.\n\nThe robot patrols 4 office waypoints (Lobby, Corridor, Office, Storage), navigates via Nav2, and verifies ArUco markers (IDs 100-103, DICT_4X4_1000) at each checkpoint. Results are logged to CSV with images.\n\n## Build & Test Commands\n\nAll commands run from `~/ros2_ws`:\n\n```bash\ncolcon build --symlink-install                                    # build all\ncolcon build --symlink-install --packages-select <package>        # build one package\nsource install/setup.bash                                         # source after every build\ncolcon test --packages-select aruco_markers                       # run aruco tests (GTest)\naruco_markers/scripts/unit_test.sh                                # run aruco unit tests directly\naruco_markers/scripts/format.sh                                   # C++ formatting (ament_uncrustify)\n```\n\n## Launch Sequence (4 terminals, source workspace in each)\n\n```bash\n# T1: Simulation\nros2 launch unitree_go2_sim unitree_go2_launch.py world:=office_patrol.sdf\n\n# T2: Navigation (AMCL + Nav2)\nros2 launch unitree_go2_sim nav2_patrol_launch.py map:=~/ros2_ws/src/unitree_go2_ros2/maps/office_patrol_map.yaml\n\n# T3: ArUco detection\nros2 launch unitree_go2_sim aruco_detection_launch.py\n\n# T4: Patrol controller\nros2 run unitree_go2_sim patrol_controller.py\n```\n\nOr use the all-in-one script: `~/ros2_ws/src/Scripts/go2_autonav.sh`\n\nKill everything: `GO2_KILL_GZ=1 ~/ros2_ws/src/Scripts/go2_kill_terms.sh`\n\n## Package Structure\n\n- **`aruco_markers/aruco_markers/`** — C++ node for ArUco detection using OpenCV. Source in `src/`, headers in `include/aruco_markers/`, tests in `test/` (GTest).\n- **`aruco_markers/aruco_markers_msgs/`** — Custom messages: `Marker` (id, pose, pixel coords) and `MarkerArray`.\n- **`unitree_go2_ros2/unitree_go2_sim/`** — Launch files (`launch/`), Python scripts (`scripts/` — patrol_controller, camera_info_publisher), config YAML (`config/`).\n- **`unitree_go2_ros2/unitree_go2_description/`** — URDF/xacro (`urdf/`), Gazebo worlds (`worlds/`), ArUco marker models (`models/`), meshes.\n- **`unitree_go2_ros2/champ/`** + **`champ_base/`** — CHAMP quadruped locomotion framework and ROS drivers (controller, state estimation, EKF).\n- **`unitree_go2_ros2/config/`** — Nav2 params (`nav2_go2_params.yaml`), SLAM params, RViz configs.\n- **`Scripts/`** — Bash launcher scripts: `go2_autonav.sh` (all-in-one), `go2_launcher.sh` (base launcher), `go2_nav2_map.sh` (nav2+map), `go2_patrol_nav.sh` (patrol nav), `go2_kill_terms.sh` (kill all), `go2_reset_localization.sh` (reset AMCL pose).\n\n## Architecture\n\n**Control stack**: Gazebo Harmonic → ros_gz_bridge → CHAMP quadruped controller → Dual EKF filters → Nav2 (AMCL + DWB local planner)\n\n**TF tree**: `map` → (AMCL) → `odom` → (EKF) → `base_link` → `base_footprint` → leg links\n\n**Sensor pipeline**: Velodyne PointCloud2 → `pointcloud_to_laserscan` → `/scan` (LaserScan) → Nav2 costmaps\n\n**ArUco pipeline**: `/rgb_image` + `/rgb_image/camera_info` → `aruco_markers` node → `/aruco/markers` (MarkerArray) + `/aruco/result` (debug image)\n\n**Patrol controller** (`patrol_controller.py`): Python node using `nav2_simple_commander.BasicNavigator`. Navigates waypoints, polls `/aruco/markers`, retries up to 3 times with optional in-place rotation, logs to CSV at `~/inspection_data/`.\n\n## Coding Conventions\n\n- **Python**: PEP 8, 4-space indent, `snake_case` functions/vars, `CamelCase` classes\n- **C++**: Format with `aruco_markers/scripts/format.sh` (ament_uncrustify)\n- **ROS 2**: Package names `lowercase_with_underscores`, topics `/lowercase/with/slashes`\n- **All packages**: `ament_cmake` build system\n\n## Commit Style\n\nShort imperative summaries (e.g., \"Add ...\", \"Fix ...\", \"Adjust ...\"). Add body for multi-area changes. Include affected packages and commands run (`colcon build`, `colcon test`).\n\n## Key Configuration Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `unitree_go2_sim/config/nav2_go2_params.yaml` | Nav2 parameters (AMCL, DWB, costmaps) — canonical source (`unitree_go2_ros2/config/` has symlinks) |\n| `unitree_go2_sim/config/patrol_waypoints.yaml` | Patrol waypoints with marker IDs |\n| `unitree_go2_sim/config/gait/gait.yaml` | Quadruped gait parameters |\n| `unitree_go2_sim/config/ros_control/ros_control.yaml` | Joint controllers (250 Hz) |\n| `unitree_go2_description/worlds/office_patrol.sdf` | Gazebo world with ArUco markers |\n\n## Important Runtime Notes\n\n- Always `source install/setup.bash` in every terminal before launching\n- Set `GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH` to include `unitree_go2_description/models` if marker models are missing (launcher scripts handle this)\n- Set initial pose in RViz (\"2D Pose Estimate\") before starting patrol\n- ArUco markers are 300mm code on 340mm panel (20mm quiet zone), placed at ground level\n- Waypoints are offset ~0.9m from marker positions to stay outside Nav2 inflation radius\n- Robot radius: 0.30m, max velocity: 0.30 m/s forward, 0.50 rad/s rotation (tuned to CHAMP gait limits)\n- Inspection output: `~/inspection_data/inspection_log.csv` + `~/inspection_data/images/`\n","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ceb9380f-b056-475b-a59b-cb1f38a47cca"}
